# ----------------------------------------------------------
# <type>(<scope>): <subject> (max 72 chars)
#
# <body> (explain WHAT changed and WHY, wrap at 72 chars)
#
# <footer> (refs, closes, breaking changes)
# ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Activate once per clone:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Types:
#   feat:     New feature
#   fix:      Bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation
#   style:    Code style (formatting)
#   refactor: Code refactoring
#   perf:     Performance
#   test:     Tests
#   build:    Build/tooling/deps
#   ci:       CI/CD
#   chore:    Other (version bumps, housekeeping)
#   revert:   Revert a previous commit
#
# Scope (optional): affected area, e.g.
#   sync, server, tracker, storage, ui, commands, docs, memory-bank
#
# Subject: imperative mood, no trailing period, lowercase first letter ok
#
# Examples:
#   feat(sync): implement pull loop with cursor persistence
#   fix(storage): keep soft-deleted sessions out of local statistics
#   docs(memory-bank): record sync engine design decisions
#   chore(release): bump version to 0.1.0
#
# Footer tags:
#   Closes: #123
#   Fixes: #456
#   BREAKING CHANGE: migration guide
#
# NEVER add AI attribution or co-author trailers.
# ----------------------------------------------------------
